WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Hello there.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.960
We will now focus on data storytelling.

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:12.840
Data storytelling is effectively communicating insights from a dataset using narratives and visualizations.

4
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.000
There are four aspects of great data storytelling.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.920
The first is accurate and complete data.

6
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.320
This helps establish trust with your stakeholders.

7
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.520
The second is a good design that provides clarity and is consistent.

8
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.600
The third is context.

9
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:34.920
Context involves explaining goals and customizing the message based on the audience.

10
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.800
The final aspect is the narrative.

11
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.800
Any dashboard or report should explain the next steps or the call to action.

12
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:49.640
Let us look at the multiple hats you must wear to tell a great data story.

13
00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.960
You have done an excellent job so far.

14
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.840
Now, it is time to put on a consultant's hat.

15
00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:01.160
This involves communicating the insights you gleaned to Whiskique's management.

16
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:07.920
They are business users and immediately understand terms such as sales, profit, and expenses.

17
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.120
So, removing technical jargon such as table merges, data sources, or parameters will be best.

18
00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.080
Your dashboard-style pages should attempt to answer questions such as:

19
00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:19.120


20
00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.200
How will this grow my sales or profit?

21
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.640
How will this strategy improve customer satisfaction?

22
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.640
How can I save on shipping costs?

23
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:34.400
Your deliverable will consist of three dashboard-style pages.

24
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.880
You will reuse many of the charts built in the previous exercises.

25
00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:45.880
In the executive summary dashboard-style page, you will provide key KPIs such as sales and profit.

26
00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.960
This dashboard will provide a high-level pulse of the business.

27
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:57.720
The shipping costs dashboard-style page will suggest multiple strategies to reduce shipping costs.

28
00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.440
The growth opportunities dashboard-style page will provide specific

29
00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:07.640
recommendations on how Whiskique can grow sales using cross-sell promotions.

30
00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:11.760
Let us now start building your data story.

